# CI/CD with GitHub Actions for NASA Anomaly Detection

This project demonstrates how to take a machine learning model, package it into a Flask web service, and then fully automate its build, test, and deployment using **GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines**. 

## Keywords : Kubernetes services, GitHub runner environments, security tokens, `act`

Project Structure
nasa-anomaly/
|----CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
|----DataReadme.txt
|----Dockerfile 
|----README
|----requirements.txt
|----test_FD001.txt
|----train_FD001.txt
|----.github/workflows/
    |----ci_cd.yml    
|----k8s/manifests/
    |----deployment.yml
    |----service.yml
|----output/
    |----TestAnomalyResults
    |----TrainAnomalyResults
    |----plot/

* Dockerfile
    Defines the container environment using python:3.9-slim as the base image.
        The Dockerfile has comments included for every execution

* requirements.txt list all dependencies in PyPI version only

* train_FD001.txt   
    Holds the training data

* test_FD001.txt
    Hold the test data

* DataReadme
    Information on training and test data

* ci_cd.yml
    Workflow for Github actions

* Deployment.yml
    Manages replicas, restart policy

* Service.yml
    Defines a ClusterIP Service that exposes the Flask API within the Kubernetes cluster

* output
    *TestAnomalyResults
        Anomalies predicted in test data
    *TrainAnomalyResults
        Anomalies predicted in train data
    *plots/
        Plots with anomalies and correct data points

* CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
    ML script to train the model and classify the data points

